<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n100919" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνοχ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one that holds together</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τῶν ἐνύλων εἰδῶν ς. θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					5.165d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
			</span></i>
			<i>in R.</i><i><span class="en">
				2.307K.
			</span></i>, al.: pl., <i>maintainers</i>, a certain order of gods in
			Neo-Platonism, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>in Prm.</u>
				p.494S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				96
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>one who holds the loyalty</i> of others, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρωπος ς. καὶ ἑνωτικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Horap.
					2.116
				</span></i>
			.</div>
